The project's own work (the build system and tools in tools/, configure.py,
nix/, the configuration in config/ and the documentation) is licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or any later version; see
COPYING for the full text.

The code in src/ and include/ is not covered by that licence. It is a
reconstruction, by reverse engineering, of the program code of Theme
Hospital's HOSPITAL.EXE (1997), and of the third-party code linked into it:

  - the game and Bullfrog's libraries, (C) Bullfrog Productions Ltd /
    Electronic Arts Inc.;
  - the Miles Sound System, (C) RAD Game Tools / Miles Design;
  - RAD Smacker, (C) RAD Game Tools;
  - the Watcom C/C++ 10.x runtime library, (C) Watcom International /
    Sybase.

No rights in that code are claimed, and none are granted by this file; it
remains the property of its respective owners. Names, comments and
documentation that contributors added to those files are offered under the
GPL to the extent the contributors hold any rights in them.

The project contains no game assets and no original binaries: building it
needs your own copy of the game. It is distributed without charge and in
good faith, for those who own Theme Hospital and want to study, preserve
and document it. Should the original copyright holders object, we will take
down the code they have the rights to.
